@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="hero" style="min-height: auto; padding: 3rem 1rem 1.5rem;">
    <div class="hero-content" style="max-width: 1000px; width: 100%;">
        <h1 class="hero-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="verse-box text-start" style="max-width: 100%;">
            <p style="color: #ddd; margin-bottom: 0;">England Technologies LLC collects only the information needed to schedule and perform your service, never sells it, and deletes copies of your files after the work is done. Effective October 9, 2026.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="container pb-5" style="max-width: 1000px;">
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">1. Information I Collect</h2>
        <p><strong>Booking details.</strong> When you book, the form asks for your name, email, phone number, address, city, zip code, a description of the problem, when it started, how you prefer to be contacted, and any notes you choose to add.</p>
        <p><strong>Messages.</strong> If you email, text, or call me, I keep the messages and any details you share in them.</p>
        <p><strong>Website data.</strong> Like most websites, the web server may record basic technical information, such as your IP address, browser type, the pages requested, and the date and time. I use it to keep the site secure and working.</p>
        <p><strong>Payment information.</strong> Payments are processed by Stripe. I do not see or store your full card number or wallet details. I receive a record of the payment, such as your name, email address, the amount, and the last four digits of your card. Stripe's use of your payment information is covered by its own privacy policy.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">2. How I Use It</h2>
        <p>I use your information to schedule and confirm appointments, contact you about your service, give you a plan and cost before work begins, perform the work, handle billing and business records, keep the website secure, follow the law, and resolve disputes. I do not send marketing messages unless you ask for them.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">3. Your Files and Devices During a Service</h2>
        <p>When I work on a device, I may be able to see files, photos, messages, saved passwords, and accounts. I look only at what the work needs. I copy personal files only when the service calls for it, such as a backup, a migration, or an image of a drive being recovered, and I do not share them with anyone.</p>
        <p>I do not keep your passwords. Master passwords, recovery codes, and backup codes stay with you.</p>
        <p>If I see personal information by accident while working, I keep it confidential. The one exception is illegal content, which is covered in the <a href="/terms" style="color: #00bfff;">Terms and Conditions</a>.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">4. Sharing</h2>
        <p>My booking system and email run on servers that I operate myself, so your information stays under my control. I do not sell or rent your information. I share information only in these cases:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>With a service I use to deliver messages, process payments, or run a support session, such as email, text messaging, or remote-support software, and only what that service needs.</li>
            <li>When the law requires it, such as a court order or a legal request.</li>
            <li>To protect safety, prevent fraud, or defend my legal rights.</li>
            <li>If the business is sold or transferred, in which case business records may move to the new owner.</li>
        </ul>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">5. Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p>Copies of your files that I make during a service, including backups, migration copies, and images of drives, are deleted once you confirm your files are safe. They are deleted no later than 15 days after the service, unless you ask me in writing to keep them longer, at which point I will keep the data a maximum of 60 days after the service. An automated timer will delete the data after 60 days, and there will be no extension after the 60 days are up. There is no way to undo or stop this timer.</p>
        <p>The only exception to this rule is in the event that law enforcement gets involved. In this exception, the data will be kept as long as law enforcement needs the data and will be deleted immediately after involvement with law enforcement ends.</p>
        <p>If I take ownership of equipment that was left unpaid or uncollected, as described in the <a href="/terms" style="color: #00bfff;">Terms and Conditions</a>, I securely erase any data on it before it is reused, recycled, or disposed of.</p>
        <p>Booking and billing records are kept for as long as needed for business, tax, and legal purposes. Messages are kept while they are useful for supporting you.</p>
        <p>You can ask me to delete your booking information at any time. I may need to keep some records where the law requires it.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="card mb-4"><div class="card-body" style="color: #ddd;">
        <h2 class="h4" style="color: #00bfff;">6. Security, Cookies, and Your Choices</h2>
        <p>I use reasonable safeguards to protect your information, such as password protection, limited access to my systems, and keeping software up to date. No method of storing or sending data is completely secure, so I cannot promise absolute security. If a breach affects your information, I will notify you as the law requires.</p>
        <p>The booking system uses cookies or similar storage that it needs to work, such as keeping your session while you book. I do not use advertising or tracking cookies.</p>
        <p>You can ask to see, correct, or delete the information I hold about you, or ask me to stop contacting you by email or text. Send the request through the Contact page at <a href="/contactus" style="color: #00bfff;">techsupport.englandtechnologies.net/contactus</a>.</p>
        <p>My services are for adults 18 and older. I do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18 through this website.</p>
        <p>I may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it was last changed.</p>
    </div></div>
</section>
